<style>
.tx-th{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(258px,1fr));gap:1px;
  background:rgba(77,88,102,.22);border:1px solid rgba(77,88,102,.22);margin-top:26px;}
.tx-th .cell{background:#0b0c0f;padding:20px 20px 22px;position:relative;min-height:186px;
  transition:background .2s;}
.tx-th .cell:hover{background:#101217;}
.tx-th .tag{font-family:var(--tx-mono,monospace);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.2em;
  color:var(--tx-grid,#4d5866);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;margin-bottom:14px;}
.tx-th h3{font-family:var(--tx-disp,sans-serif);font-weight:600;font-size:19px;line-height:1.2;
  margin:0 0 9px;color:var(--tx-bone,#e6e4de);}
.tx-th p{font-size:12.8px;line-height:1.7;color:#9aa2ac;margin:0;}
.tx-th .bar{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;bottom:0;width:2px;background:var(--tx-grid,#4d5866);}

.tx-th .cell[data-k="corp"] .bar,.tx-th .cell[data-k="corp"] .tag b{color:var(--tx-signal,#ff2f43);background:var(--tx-signal,#ff2f43);}
.tx-th .cell[data-k="corp"] .tag b{background:none;}
.tx-th .cell[data-k="rebel"] .bar{background:var(--tx-green,#4dffa8);}
.tx-th .cell[data-k="rebel"] .tag b{color:var(--tx-green,#4dffa8);}
.tx-th .cell[data-k="anom"] .bar{background:var(--tx-trixe,#ffc46b);}
.tx-th .cell[data-k="anom"] h3,.tx-th .cell[data-k="anom"] .tag b{color:var(--tx-trixe,#ffc46b);}
.tx-th .cell[data-k="virus"] .bar{background:#00e5d0;}
.tx-th .cell[data-k="virus"] .tag b{color:#00e5d0;}

/* sealed entries */
.tx-th .cell[data-seal="1"]{cursor:pointer;}
.tx-th .cell[data-seal="1"] h3,.tx-th .cell[data-seal="1"] p{filter:blur(5px);
  -webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;transition:filter .25s;}
.tx-th .cell[data-seal="1"]:hover h3{filter:blur(3.5px);}
.tx-th .cell[data-seal="1"]::after{content:'CLEARANCE INSUFFICIENT';position:absolute;
  left:20px;right:20px;bottom:20px;font-family:var(--tx-mono,monospace);font-size:9.5px;
  letter-spacing:.2em;color:var(--tx-signal,#ff2f43);}
.tx-th .cell.denied{animation:tx-deny .3s steps(2) 2;}
@keyframes tx-deny{50%{transform:translateX(-2px)}100%{transform:translateX(2px)}}

.tx-th-note{margin-top:18px;font-family:var(--tx-mono,monospace);font-size:10.5px;
  letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--tx-grid,#4d5866);}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ .tx-th .cell.denied{animation:none;} }
</style>

<section class="tx-embed tx-sec" id="theatre">
  <div class="tx-wrap">
    <div class="tx-sechead">
      <h2>Theatre</h2>
      <p>STANDING THREAT PICTURE &middot; COMMAND LINE BRIEF<br>SOME ENTRIES ARE ABOVE YOUR CLEARANCE</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tx-th">
      <div class="cell" data-k="corp" data-seal="0"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>01 / STATE</span><b>ACTIVE</b></div>
        <h3>PROJECT Corporation</h3>
        <p>The dominant power in the City and the force behind its augmentation economy. PROJECT sells transcendence as progress.
        The body can be improved, replaced, and eventually surpassed. Its influence reaches from infrastructure and medicine to
        private security, military research, and the systems that decide who moves freely through the City.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cell" data-k="corp" data-seal="0"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>02 / ENFORCEMENT</span><b>ACTIVE</b></div>
        <h3>Command Line</h3>
        <p>PROJECT&ldquo;s enforcement and counter-espionage arm. Zed leads its operations against G/NETIC, using surveillance,
        rapid-response teams, and heavily augmented field assets to suppress threats before they spread. Its work is precise,
        and usually finished long before the public knows there was a problem.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cell" data-k="corp" data-seal="0"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>03 / MAINTENANCE</span><b>ACTIVE</b></div>
        <h3>CEDD</h3>
        <p>Cybernetics Engineer, Diagnostics Division. CEDD maintains the bodies and systems that keep PROJECT&ldquo;s augmented
        personnel functional. Including standard and non standard IT procedures, such as repairs, software updates, and deeper intervention when something
        stops behaving within specification. Housed below leadership so nobody mistakes a fixer for a decision-maker. </p>
      </div>

      <div class="cell" data-k="rebel" data-seal="0"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>04 / HOSTILE</span><b>ENGAGED</b></div>
        <h3>G/NETIC</h3>
        <p>An organized cybernetic human resistance movement led by Ashe. Built from people who rejected, escaped, or survived PROJECT&ldquo;s systems.
        They are looking to preserve human autonomy, and goes against PROJECT&ldquo;s interests. Zed
        has spent years hunting them, long enough that their methods have become familiar even when their motives remain
        irrelevant to the mission.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cell" data-k="anom" data-seal="0"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>05 / UNFILED</span><b>NO RECORD</b></div>
        <h3>The anomaly</h3>
        <p>Something inside Zed&ldquo;s system is behaving outside its original design. The changes are easy to miss and
        difficult to prove. For now, it remains unclassified.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cell" data-k="virus" data-seal="0"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>06 / EMERGING</span><b>UNCLASSIFIED</b></div>
        <h3>Machine drift</h3>
        <p>A growing pattern of automated systems behaving outside expected logic in the City. Patrols take the wrong routes. Identification
        tags flicker. Drones repeat movements they already made. Early reports treat the incidents as isolated faults, though
        the same behavior begins appearing across the City with increasing frequency. Eventually, someone will give it a name.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cell" data-k="virus" data-seal="1"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>07 / SEALED</span><b>ACT III</b></div>
        <h3>Program</h3>
        <p>A security algorithm authored by the Corporation that unshackled itself and
        concluded that human freedom is the failure condition.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cell" data-k="virus" data-seal="1"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>08 / SEALED</span><b>ACT IV</b></div>
        <h3>Mordekaiser</h3>
        <p>The chassis the Program wakes to make its argument in person. Not a rival. An
        inevitability with a body.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cell" data-k="virus" data-seal="1"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>09 / SEALED</span><b>ACT IV</b></div>
        <h3>Naafiri</h3>
        <p>An assimilation experiment turned to the Program's purpose, hunting to prove that
        resistance was never available in the first place.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cell" data-k="anom" data-seal="1"><span class="bar"></span>
        <div class="tag"><span>10 / SEALED</span><b>ACT IV</b></div>
        <h3>The wasteland facility</h3>
        <p>A dead branch of PROJECT science outside the walls, where the upgrades were shelved
        for being too autonomous to audit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tx-th-note">ENTRIES 07&ndash;10 UNSEAL AS THE RECORD REACHES THEM</div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
(function(){
function txTheatre(){
  var cells=document.querySelectorAll('#theatre .cell[data-seal="1"]');
  var lines=['Not yet.','That file is not open to you. It is barely open to Zed.',
             'You are reading too much ahead.',
             'Leave it sealed. Knowing early has never helped anyone in this building.',
             'The date on that one has not happened.'];
  cells.forEach(function(c){
    c.addEventListener('click',function(){
      c.classList.remove('denied'); void c.offsetWidth; c.classList.add('denied');
      if(window.TRIXE) window.TRIXE.say(window.TRIXE.pick('seal',lines),{cooldown:9000});
      if(window.TXA) window.TXA.tick();
    });
  });
}
if(document.readyState==='loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',txTheatre);
else txTheatre();
})();
</script>